{
 "result": "maze.py is built and passes all three samples (in-0 \u2192 2008, in-1 \u2192 -1, in-2 \u2192 78). It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a wall border, and runs a level-by-level BFS over a flat bytearray, stopping as soon as E is reached and printing -1 if the frontier empties. The assay registered a baseline of 3.87355 with 9.8% noise. One variant that tested E once per BFS level scored 4.016 against an incumbent of 3.962, which is inside noise, so the incumbent was kept. I am resting here rather than spending more energy on small micro-optimisations that the noise floor is likely to hide.",
